// design 186 unit 7 tier (c), pinned by DF-307a: a String is not a constant
// initializer, and the hint says so in the same breath as the function call
// (`static_non_const.saw`) and the user `init` body
// (`static_user_init_not_const.saw`).
//
// This row exists because DF-307a WIDENED the tier — `sizeof`/`alignof` of a
// primitive folds now, and a leaf may name an earlier static of ANY type — and
// a widening owes a control for every clause it did NOT touch. A String is a
// refcounted heap value built at run time; a static is image bytes.
//
// Two errors, deliberately: the const-init rule and design 41's own rule that a
// static may not own a resource. Neither is redundant — the second is what
// would still refuse the declaration if somebody made string literals foldable.
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: static `GREETING` must be initialized by a compile-time constant
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: neither does a function call, a String or any heap type
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: owns a resource (Deinit)

static GREETING: String = "hello"

func main() { print(GREETING) }
